            <ArticleTitle>Thoracic disc protrusion. (Analysis of 8 cases).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>251-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Eight cases of thoracic disc protrusion, observed over a period of four years, are reported. The literature was also reviewed. It is emphasized that in chronic midline disc protrusions a careful laminectomy without removal of the disc can give satisfactory results.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
